//@version=6
// =====================================================================
// MULTI-STRATEGY CONFIRMATION SYSTEM
//
// Seven reads of the same chart, each switchable, and a trade only when
// enough INDEPENDENT ones agree:
//
//   STRUCTURE family
//     1. RANGE BREAKOUT   — close beyond an N-bar range
//     2. BOS              — close beyond the last swing, WITH the bias
//   REJECTION family
//     3. S/R PUSHBACK     — rejection approaching a swing pivot
//     4. LIQUIDITY SWEEP  — wick THROUGH a swing, close back inside
//   ZONE family
//     5. ORDER BLOCK      — rejection inside the base of an impulse
//     6. FAIR VALUE GAP   — rejection inside a 3-bar imbalance
//   SESSION family
//     7. ORB              — break of the session's opening range
//
//   Filters (no direction of their own, so they gate rather than vote):
//     displacement, close strength, hold-for-N-bars, relative volume,
//     volume surge, volume delta, session window

// FAKEOUT CONTROL — THE THREE THAT ACTUALLY WORK
// A fakeout is a break that closes back inside. Three filters attack it
// from different angles and they stack:
//
//   1. DISPLACEMENT. The breaking bar's body must exceed a multiple of
//      ATR. A real break leaves a body; a fakeout drifts across.
//   2. CLOSE STRENGTH. The close must sit in the top (or bottom)
//      `closeStrength` of the bar's own range. A break that closes
//      mid-bar left a long wick against itself, which is the fakeout
//      signature written into the candle.
//   3. HOLD FOR N BARS. The strongest of the three, and the only one
//      that is not a guess: the signal is WITHHELD for `holdBars` bars
//      and fires only if price is still beyond the level when they have
//      printed. A fakeout is by definition gone by then.
//
// Hold costs you the first N bars of the move, which is the honest
// trade: you cannot both act immediately and know the break held. It
// applies to the STRUCTURE family, because that is where fakeouts live —
// rejections and zone entries are already close-confirmed against a
// level and have nothing to fake out of.

// MARKET DEPTH IS NOT AVAILABLE, AND NOTHING HERE PRETENDS OTHERWISE
// Pine Script cannot read the order book. There is no bid size, no ask
// size, no DOM, no Level 2 — TradingView does not expose any of it to
// scripts, on any plan. Any indicator claiming to show "institutional
// order flow" from a TradingView chart is inferring it from price and
// volume, not reading it.
//
// The closest real substitute is VOLUME DELTA, and this script offers
// it: `ta.requestVolumeDelta` drops to a lower timeframe and splits
// volume into the part that traded on upticks and the part on downticks.
// That is genuine directional information and it is still an ESTIMATE
// built from bars, not a read of resting orders. On spot XAUUSD it is
// estimated from tick counts, which makes it an estimate of an estimate;
// on GC1! it is built from real traded size.
//
// WHY FAMILIES, AND WHY THIS IS THE IMPORTANT PART
// Most of these are computed from the same swing pivots. A range
// breakout, a BOS and a swept high are three descriptions of one thing:
// price left a level. Counting them as three confirmations is counting
// one observation three times, and it makes `minConfirmations` a number
// that no longer means what it says — the more strategies you switch on,
// the EASIER the filter gets, which is the opposite of the intent.
//
// So each family casts at most ONE vote. Two votes means two genuinely
// different kinds of evidence: something structural happened AND price
// rejected a level, or a zone held AND structure broke. `capFamilies`
// turns this off if you want to see the difference; leaving it off is
// how a confirmation system quietly becomes a single-signal system with
// extra steps.
//
// ALL SEVEN ARE EVENTS
// Each is true on the bar the thing happens and false afterwards, so a
// vote count is a count of things that OCCURRED. An earlier version
// carried a trend-following slot (Supertrend, then DI/ADX) and it was a
// STATE — true for as long as the trend lasted — which meant "2 of 4"
// could be satisfied by one event plus a standing condition. It also
// vetoed pullback entries, since an ATR band flips exactly when price
// retests support. Removing it was the fix; do not add another state.
//
// DISPLACEMENT
// The single best filter on a structural break. An institutional move
// leaves a large body, not a drift across the line. `requireDisplacement`
// demands the breaking bar's body exceed `displacementAtr` x ATR, which
// discards most false breaks. It applies to the STRUCTURE family only —
// a rejection is not supposed to be violent.
//
// WHAT LAGS, AND WHY THAT IS NOT A BUG
// A swing pivot is not confirmed until `pivotRight` bars have printed
// after it, so `ta.pivothigh()` returns a value already shifted back by
// that many bars. That is correct — the script cannot see a pivot before
// the chart could have — and it means every structure signal here is
// late by design. Reducing pivotRight makes them arrive sooner and makes
// more of them false. There is no setting that gives you early AND right.
//
// REPAINTING
// Signals are evaluated on bar close. Do not enable "calc on every tick",
// which lets a vote appear and vanish inside a bar. The breakout range
// uses [1] so it excludes the live bar — a range containing the bar being
// tested moves with price and nothing ever breaks it.
//
// ENTRIES ARE LIMIT ORDERS, AND THEY EXPIRE
// A signal places a limit order `entryAtrMult` x ATR from the level that
// justified it — a retest, not a chase. If the retest price is not on the
// correct side of the market the order is NOT placed, because a buy limit
// at or above the market fills instantly at the market. An unfilled order
// is cancelled after `orderExpiryBars`, since one left alive fills days
// later in a setup that no longer exists.
//
// THIS IS A BACKTEST INSTRUMENT
// TradingView fills every limit order price touches, with no queue, no
// partial fills and no slippage beyond what you configure. Real fills are
// worse. Treat a losing backtest as conclusive and a winning one as a
// reason to go and measure the spread you actually pay.
//
// VOLUME IS A FILTER, AND ON GOLD IT IS TICK VOLUME
// Volume has no direction, so it cannot vote — it gates. `useVolume`
// requires the signal bar to trade above `volMult` x its own recent
// average.
//
// Read it for what it is. XAUUSD from a spot CFD feed reports TICK COUNT,
// not contracts: it measures how often the price was requoted, not how
// much was transacted. It tracks real futures volume well enough to be
// useful as a participation proxy and badly enough that calling a spike
// "institutional accumulation" would be a story, not a measurement. On a
// futures symbol (GC1!) the same input is real traded size.
//
// WHY CHoCH WAS REMOVED
// It fired and changed nothing. Ported to Python and run over 269 real
// daily bars it triggered three times, and a 20-bar range breakout fired
// on all three of those bars — so the structure vote was already cast and
// toggling CHoCH could not alter a single decision. A swing low usually
// IS the recent range low, which makes the two fire together. The
// FIRED/SOLO columns exist so the next redundant idea is visible in one
// glance instead of one A/B test.
//
// ON VERY HIGH WIN RATES
// This system will not produce one, and a version that did would be worse.
// Win rate and profit are close to independent: a 25% win rate at 10.9:1
// and a 48% win rate at 3.3:1 were measured on this same instrument and
// the 25% version made more money. Systems advertising 95%+ get there by
// risking thirty to make one, which hides the loss rather than removing
// it. For FEWER, BETTER trades set minConfirmations to 3 and switch on
// displacement, volume and a session — that is selectivity, which is a
// real thing, rather than a win rate, which is a ratio you can rig.
// =====================================================================

strategy("Multi-Strategy Confirmation",
     overlay              = true,
     initial_capital      = 100000,
     default_qty_type     = strategy.percent_of_equity,
     default_qty_value    = 100,
     pyramiding           = 0,
     calc_on_order_fills  = false,
     process_orders_on_close = true,
     commission_type      = strategy.commission.percent,
     commission_value     = 0.03,
     slippage             = 2,
     max_boxes_count      = 500)

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ inputs
grpC = "Confirmation"
minConfirmations = input.int(2, "Votes required to enter", minval=1, maxval=4, group=grpC,
     tooltip="Votes are counted per FAMILY when capFamilies is on, so the ceiling is 4: structure, rejection, zone, session.")
capFamilies = input.bool(true, "One vote per family (recommended)", group=grpC,
     tooltip="Correlated signals are computed from the same pivots. Without this, switching on more strategies makes the filter LOOSER, not tighter, because one observation gets counted several times.")
blockOnOpposition = input.bool(true, "Block if any family opposes", group=grpC)

grpF = "Filters"
requireDisplacement = input.bool(false, "Structural breaks need displacement", group=grpF,
     tooltip="The breaking bar's body must exceed displacementAtr x ATR. Applies to the STRUCTURE family only — a rejection is not supposed to be violent.")
displacementAtr = input.float(0.8, "Displacement body (x ATR)", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group=grpF)

useVolume = input.bool(false, "Signal bar needs above-average volume", group=grpF,
     tooltip="A participation filter, not a vote — volume has no direction. On spot XAUUSD this is TICK COUNT, not contracts: it measures requote frequency, a decent proxy for activity and not a measurement of size. On GC1! it is real traded volume.")
volMult = input.float(1.5, "Volume vs its average (x)", minval=0.5, step=0.1, group=grpF)
volLen = input.int(20, "Volume average length", minval=2, group=grpF)
useVolSurge = input.bool(false, "Require a volume SURGE, not just above average", group=grpF,
     tooltip="A z-score: how many standard deviations above its own mean this bar traded. Above-average volume is common; a 2-sigma surge is a step change, which is what 'sudden' means numerically.")
volZ = input.float(2.0, "Surge z-score", minval=0.5, step=0.25, group=grpF)
useVolDelta = input.bool(false, "Require volume delta to agree with the trade", group=grpF,
     tooltip="The closest thing to order flow that Pine can see. Drops to a lower timeframe and splits volume into uptick and downtick parts. It is an ESTIMATE from bars, not a read of the order book — Pine has no access to the book at all. Errors if the lower timeframe is not finer than the chart's.")
deltaTf = input.timeframe("1", "Volume delta lower timeframe", group=grpF)
useSession = input.bool(false, "Trade only inside a session", group=grpF)
sessionSpec = input.session("0700-1600", "Session (exchange time)", group=grpF,
     tooltip="London plus the New York overlap in UTC terms. Check your chart's timezone — this is evaluated in exchange time, not yours.")

grpK = "Fakeout control"
closeStrength = input.float(0.0, "Break close within its own range (0-1)", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=grpK,
     tooltip="0 disables. 0.6 means a bullish break must close in the top 40% of its bar. A break closing mid-bar left a long wick against itself, which is what a fakeout looks like in the candle.")
holdBars = input.int(0, "Break must hold for N bars", minval=0, maxval=20, group=grpK,
     tooltip="The strongest fakeout filter and the only one that is not a guess. The signal is withheld this many bars and fires only if price is STILL beyond the level. Costs you the first N bars of the move — you cannot both act immediately and know the break held. 0 disables.")

grpP = "Swing pivots (feeds structure, S/R and sweeps)"
pivotLeft = input.int(10, "Pivot left bars", minval=1, group=grpP)
pivotRight = input.int(10, "Pivot right bars", minval=1, group=grpP,
     tooltip="Also the lag: a pivot is not confirmed until this many bars have printed after it.")

grp1 = "1. Range breakout (structure)"
useBreakout = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grp1)
breakoutLen = input.int(20, "Range lookback (bars)", minval=2, group=grp1)

grp2 = "2. BOS - break of structure (structure)"
useBos = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grp2,
     tooltip="Close beyond the last swing in the direction the structure is already going. Continuation.")

grp3 = "3. S/R pushback (rejection)"
useSR = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grp3)
srTolAtr = input.float(0.5, "Touch tolerance (x ATR)", minval=0.05, step=0.05, group=grp3)

grp4 = "4. Liquidity sweep (rejection)"
useSweep = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grp4,
     tooltip="The wick trades THROUGH the swing and the close comes back inside — stops taken, price rejected. Stricter than a pushback, which only requires price to approach.")

grp5 = "5. Order block (zone)"
useZones = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grp5,
     tooltip="The base an impulse departed from: when a bar's body exceeds impulseAtr x ATR, the bar BEFORE it becomes the zone.")
impulseAtr = input.float(1.5, "Impulse body (x ATR)", minval=0.5, step=0.1, group=grp5)

grp6 = "6. Fair value gap (zone)"
useFvg = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grp6,
     tooltip="A three-bar imbalance: bar 1's high below bar 3's low leaves a range price traded through without trading in. Entry is the return to it.")
fvgMinAtr = input.float(0.25, "Minimum gap size (x ATR)", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=grp6)

grp7 = "7. Opening range breakout (session)"
useOrb = input.bool(false, "Enabled", group=grp7,
     tooltip="The session's first minutes set a range; the break of it is the signal. Fires at most once per side per day by construction, which is the cheapest way to get from many trades to few.")
orbSession = input.session("0800-0830", "Opening range window (exchange time)", group=grp7,
     tooltip="Gold: 0800-0830 is the London open, 1330-1400 the New York cash open. Check your chart's timezone — this is exchange time, not yours.")

grpZ = "Zone handling (order blocks and FVGs)"
zoneMaxAge = input.int(200, "Zone max age (bars)", minval=10, group=grpZ)
zoneMaxCount = input.int(6, "Zones kept per side per type", minval=1, maxval=20, group=grpZ)
drawZones = input.bool(true, "Draw zones", group=grpZ)

grpE = "Entry"
entryAtrMult = input.float(0.1, "Limit offset from level (x ATR)", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=grpE)
orderExpiryBars = input.int(5, "Cancel unfilled order after (bars)", minval=1, group=grpE)

grpR = "Risk"
atrLen = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval=1, group=grpR)
stopAtrMult = input.float(1.5, "Initial stop beyond level (x ATR)", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group=grpR)
breakevenR = input.float(1.0, "Lock breakeven at (R multiple)", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group=grpR)
useTrailing = input.bool(true, "Trail the stop after breakeven", group=grpR)
trailTightness = input.int(2, "Trail tightness after breakeven (1 loose - 5 tight)", minval=1, maxval=5, group=grpR)
takeProfitR = input.float(0.0, "Take profit at (R multiple, 0 = off)", minval=0.0, step=0.5, group=grpR,
     tooltip="Needed when the trail is off. With no trail AND no target the only exits are the initial stop and the breakeven stop, so every trade is a loss or a scratch and none can ever win.")

grpA = "Webhook alerts"
alertSecret = input.string("", "Ingest secret", group=grpA)
alertQty = input.int(1, "Quantity to send", minval=1, group=grpA)

// ------------------------------------------------------------------- atr
atr = ta.atr(atrLen)
atrOk = not na(atr) and atr > 0
body = math.abs(close - open)

trailAtrMult = switch trailTightness
    1 => 3.0
    2 => 2.5
    3 => 2.0
    4 => 1.5
    => 1.0

inSession = not useSession or not na(time(timeframe.period, sessionSpec))

// Volume gates; it never votes, because it has no direction. na volume on a
// feed that does not report it must not silently pass the filter, so an
// absent series fails the test rather than being treated as sufficient.
volAvg = ta.sma(volume, volLen)
volSd = ta.stdev(volume, volLen)
volOk = not useVolume or (not na(volume) and not na(volAvg) and volAvg > 0 and volume > volMult * volAvg)

// "Sudden" as a number. Above-average volume is common; a 2-sigma bar is a
// step change. Zero standard deviation means the series cannot support a
// z-score, so the filter fails rather than dividing by zero.
volZScore = not na(volSd) and volSd > 0 and not na(volAvg) ? (volume - volAvg) / volSd : na
volSurgeOk = not useVolSurge or (not na(volZScore) and volZScore >= volZ)

// The nearest thing to order flow Pine can reach. An ESTIMATE assembled
// from lower-timeframe bars, never a read of resting orders — see the
// header. Called unconditionally because request functions may not sit
// inside a conditional block.
[dOpen, dMax, dMin, dLast] = ta.requestVolumeDelta(deltaTf)
deltaOkLong  = not useVolDelta or (not na(dLast) and dLast > 0)
deltaOkShort = not useVolDelta or (not na(dLast) and dLast < 0)

// --------------------------------------------------------------- pivots
// Already lagged by pivotRight when they arrive, so referencing them here
// cannot see into the future.
ph = ta.pivothigh(pivotLeft, pivotRight)
pl = ta.pivotlow(pivotLeft, pivotRight)
var float lastPH = na
var float lastPL = na
if not na(ph)
    lastPH := ph
if not na(pl)
    lastPL := pl

// ------------------------------------------- STRUCTURE 1. range breakout
// [1] excludes the live bar. Without it the range contains the bar being
// tested, rises with it, and never breaks.
rangeHigh = ta.highest(high, breakoutLen)[1]
rangeLow  = ta.lowest(low, breakoutLen)[1]
brkLong  = useBreakout and not na(rangeHigh) and close > rangeHigh
brkShort = useBreakout and not na(rangeLow)  and close < rangeLow

// ------------------------------------------------- STRUCTURE 2. BOS
// One swing level produces at most ONE break event. Tracking the level
// already broken is what makes this an event rather than a state: without
// it, every subsequent close beyond the same high re-signals, and the
// "count of things that happened" becomes a count of bars.
var float brokenHigh = na
var float brokenLow = na
var int bias = 0

brokeHigh = not na(lastPH) and close > lastPH and (na(brokenHigh) or lastPH != brokenHigh)
brokeLow  = not na(lastPL) and close < lastPL and (na(brokenLow)  or lastPL != brokenLow)

// A break WITH the bias is a BOS. A break against it is a change of
// character, which is not signalled here — but the bias still flips on it,
// because that is what makes the NEXT break in the new direction a genuine
// BOS rather than a counter-trend break wearing the name. Removing the
// signal must not remove the bookkeeping.
bosLong = false
bosShort = false
if brokeHigh
    if bias >= 0
        bosLong := true
    brokenHigh := lastPH
    bias := 1
if brokeLow
    if bias <= 0
        bosShort := true
    brokenLow := lastPL
    bias := -1

bosLong  := useBos and bosLong
bosShort := useBos and bosShort

// ------------------------------------------- REJECTION 3. S/R pushback
srTol = atrOk ? srTolAtr * atr : na
srLong  = useSR and not na(lastPL) and not na(srTol) and low  <= lastPL + srTol and close > lastPL
srShort = useSR and not na(lastPH) and not na(srTol) and high >= lastPH - srTol and close < lastPH

// ---------------------------------------- REJECTION 4. liquidity sweep
// Strictly beyond the level and back, which is the difference from a
// pushback: the stops under that low were actually taken before price
// rejected. A pushback only requires price to come near.
sweepLong  = useSweep and not na(lastPL) and low  < lastPL and close > lastPL
sweepShort = useSweep and not na(lastPH) and high > lastPH and close < lastPH

// ------------------------------------------------ zone machinery (5, 6)
var array<float> obDemTop = array.new<float>()
var array<float> obDemBot = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   obDemBar = array.new<int>()
var array<float> obSupTop = array.new<float>()
var array<float> obSupBot = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   obSupBar = array.new<int>()
var array<float> fvDemTop = array.new<float>()
var array<float> fvDemBot = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   fvDemBar = array.new<int>()
var array<float> fvSupTop = array.new<float>()
var array<float> fvSupBot = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   fvSupBar = array.new<int>()
var array<box>   zoneBoxes = array.new<box>()

pushZone(array<float> tops, array<float> bots, array<int> bars, float t, float b, color col) =>
    array.push(tops, t)
    array.push(bots, b)
    array.push(bars, bar_index)
    if array.size(tops) > zoneMaxCount
        array.shift(tops)
        array.shift(bots)
        array.shift(bars)
    if drawZones
        bx = box.new(bar_index - 1, t, bar_index + 20, b,
             border_color=color.new(col, 40), bgcolor=color.new(col, 88))
        array.push(zoneBoxes, bx)
        if array.size(zoneBoxes) > 80
            box.delete(array.shift(zoneBoxes))
    true

// Walk backwards so removal does not shift an index we have yet to visit.
// Forward iteration with removal is how half a list gets skipped.
pruneZones(array<float> tops, array<float> bots, array<int> bars, bool isDemand) =>
    if array.size(tops) > 0
        for i = array.size(tops) - 1 to 0
            broken = isDemand ? close < array.get(bots, i) : close > array.get(tops, i)
            stale = bar_index - array.get(bars, i) > zoneMaxAge
            if broken or stale
                array.remove(tops, i)
                array.remove(bots, i)
                array.remove(bars, i)
    true

// The bar traded INTO the zone and closed back OUT of it. Both halves are
// needed: entering alone is price arriving, and a close inside the zone has
// not rejected anything yet. How DEEP the bar went is deliberately not
// tested — requiring the low to stay inside would discard the strongest
// signal there is, a wick clean through that closes back above.
zoneHitLong(array<float> tops) =>
    float lvl = na
    if array.size(tops) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(tops) - 1
            t = array.get(tops, i)
            if low <= t and close > t
                lvl := na(lvl) ? t : math.max(lvl, t)
    lvl

zoneHitShort(array<float> bots) =>
    float lvl = na
    if array.size(bots) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(bots) - 1
            b = array.get(bots, i)
            if high >= b and close < b
                lvl := na(lvl) ? b : math.min(lvl, b)
    lvl

// ------------------------------------------------- ZONE 5. order blocks
isImpulse = atrOk and body > impulseAtr * atr
if useZones and isImpulse and bar_index > 1
    if close > open
        pushZone(obDemTop, obDemBot, obDemBar, high[1], low[1], color.teal)
    else
        pushZone(obSupTop, obSupBot, obSupBar, high[1], low[1], color.maroon)

// ---------------------------------------------- ZONE 6. fair value gaps
// Three bars: the gap is the range bar 3 never traded into, left behind
// because bar 2 moved too fast. Measured on the CLOSED bars [1] and [3]
// so the live bar cannot create or erase one.
fvgUpSize   = atrOk and bar_index > 3 ? low[1] - high[3] : na
fvgDownSize = atrOk and bar_index > 3 ? low[3] - high[1] : na
if useFvg and not na(fvgUpSize) and fvgUpSize > fvgMinAtr * atr
    pushZone(fvDemTop, fvDemBot, fvDemBar, low[1], high[3], color.blue)
if useFvg and not na(fvgDownSize) and fvgDownSize > fvgMinAtr * atr
    pushZone(fvSupTop, fvSupBot, fvSupBar, low[3], high[1], color.orange)

if useZones
    pruneZones(obDemTop, obDemBot, obDemBar, true)
    pruneZones(obSupTop, obSupBot, obSupBar, false)
if useFvg
    pruneZones(fvDemTop, fvDemBot, fvDemBar, true)
    pruneZones(fvSupTop, fvSupBot, fvSupBar, false)

obLevelLong  = useZones ? zoneHitLong(obDemTop)  : na
obLevelShort = useZones ? zoneHitShort(obSupBot) : na
fvLevelLong  = useFvg   ? zoneHitLong(fvDemTop)  : na
fvLevelShort = useFvg   ? zoneHitShort(fvSupBot) : na
obLong  = not na(obLevelLong)
obShort = not na(obLevelShort)
fvLong  = not na(fvLevelLong)
fvShort = not na(fvLevelShort)

// ----------------------------------------------- SESSION 7. opening range
// The session's first minutes set a range and the break of it is the
// signal. At most one per side per day by construction, which is the
// cheapest way to go from many trades to few — and it is anchored to the
// CLOCK rather than to the pivots everything else here derives from, so
// its vote is genuinely independent evidence rather than the same
// observation wearing a different name.
var float orbHigh = na
var float orbLow = na
var bool orbReady = false
var bool orbLongDone = false
var bool orbShortDone = false

inOrbWindow = not na(time(timeframe.period, orbSession))
newDay = ta.change(time("D")) != 0

if newDay
    orbHigh := na
    orbLow := na
    orbReady := false
    orbLongDone := false
    orbShortDone := false

if inOrbWindow
    orbHigh := na(orbHigh) ? high : math.max(orbHigh, high)
    orbLow  := na(orbLow)  ? low  : math.min(orbLow, low)
else if not na(orbHigh)
    // The window has closed and a range exists, so it can now be broken.
    orbReady := true

orbLong  = useOrb and orbReady and not orbLongDone  and not na(orbHigh) and close > orbHigh
orbShort = useOrb and orbReady and not orbShortDone and not na(orbLow)  and close < orbLow
if orbLong
    orbLongDone := true
if orbShort
    orbShortDone := true

// ------------------------------------------------- contribution counters
// "Did this strategy do anything?" is a question the chart should answer
// rather than one you discover by toggling a switch and squinting at a
// P&L number. FIRED counts the bars a strategy triggered on. SOLO counts
// the bars where it was the ONLY one in its family to trigger — the only
// bars on which it can have changed a decision at all, since a family
// casts one vote however many of its members agree.
//
// A strategy with a healthy FIRED and SOLO of zero is fully subsumed by
// its family-mates: it costs nothing and contributes nothing. Measured on
// 269 real daily bars, CHoCH did exactly that — it fired three times and
// a 20-bar range breakout fired on all three of those bars, because a
// swing low usually IS the recent range low.
brkFired   = brkLong   or brkShort
bosFired   = bosLong   or bosShort
srFired    = srLong    or srShort
sweepFired = sweepLong or sweepShort
obFired    = obLong    or obShort
fvFired    = fvLong    or fvShort
orbFired   = orbLong   or orbShort

var int nBrk = 0
var int nBos = 0
var int nSr = 0
var int nSweep = 0
var int nOb = 0
var int nFv = 0
var int nOrb = 0
var int sBrk = 0
var int sBos = 0
var int sSr = 0
var int sSweep = 0
var int sOb = 0
var int sFv = 0
var int sOrb = 0

if barstate.isconfirmed
    if brkFired
        nBrk += 1
        sBrk += bosFired ? 0 : 1
    if bosFired
        nBos += 1
        sBos += brkFired ? 0 : 1
    if srFired
        nSr += 1
        sSr += sweepFired ? 0 : 1
    if sweepFired
        nSweep += 1
        sSweep += srFired ? 0 : 1
    if obFired
        nOb += 1
        sOb += fvFired ? 0 : 1
    if fvFired
        nFv += 1
        sFv += obFired ? 0 : 1
    if orbFired
        nOrb += 1
        // Sole member of its family, so every fire is a solo fire.
        sOrb += 1

// ------------------------------------------------- fakeout control gates
// Displacement: an institutional break leaves a body, a drift across the
// line is the false-break signature. Close strength: a break closing
// mid-bar left a long wick against itself.
displaced = not requireDisplacement or (atrOk and body > displacementAtr * atr)
barRange = high - low
closeUp = barRange > 0 ? (close - low) / barRange : 0.5
closeDn = barRange > 0 ? (high - close) / barRange : 0.5
strongUp = closeStrength <= 0 or closeUp >= closeStrength
strongDn = closeStrength <= 0 or closeDn >= closeStrength

structLevelLongRaw  = brkLong  ? rangeHigh : (bosLong  and not na(brokenHigh) ? brokenHigh : na)
structLevelShortRaw = brkShort ? rangeLow  : (bosShort and not na(brokenLow)  ? brokenLow  : na)
rawStructLong  = (brkLong  or bosLong)  and displaced and strongUp and not na(structLevelLongRaw)
rawStructShort = (brkShort or bosShort) and displaced and strongDn and not na(structLevelShortRaw)

// Hold-for-N-bars. The signal is withheld and fires only if price is STILL
// beyond the level once N bars have printed; a fakeout is gone by then. One
// break is armed at a time — a second break while one is pending would
// otherwise overwrite the level being tested and confirm against the wrong
// number.
var float armLevel = na
var int armBar = na
var int armDir = 0

bool structLong = false
bool structShort = false
float structLevelLong = na
float structLevelShort = na

if holdBars == 0
    structLong := rawStructLong
    structShort := rawStructShort
    structLevelLong := structLevelLongRaw
    structLevelShort := structLevelShortRaw
else
    if na(armBar) and (rawStructLong or rawStructShort)
        armLevel := rawStructLong ? structLevelLongRaw : structLevelShortRaw
        armBar := bar_index
        armDir := rawStructLong ? 1 : -1
    if not na(armBar) and bar_index - armBar >= holdBars
        if armDir == 1 and close > armLevel
            structLong := true
            structLevelLong := armLevel
        if armDir == -1 and close < armLevel
            structShort := true
            structLevelShort := armLevel
        // Cleared either way: a break that failed the hold is spent, not
        // re-tested on every later bar.
        armBar := na
        armDir := 0
        armLevel := na

rejLong    = srLong  or sweepLong
rejShort   = srShort or sweepShort
zoneLong   = obLong  or fvLong
zoneShort  = obShort or fvShort
sessLong   = orbLong
sessShort  = orbShort

// ------------------------------------------------------------- votes
// Per family when capped, per strategy when not. Uncapped is offered to
// show what the difference costs, not because it is a reasonable setting:
// correlated signals derived from one set of pivots make the filter looser
// the more of them you enable.
longVotesCapped  = (structLong  ? 1 : 0) + (rejLong  ? 1 : 0) + (zoneLong  ? 1 : 0) + (sessLong  ? 1 : 0)
shortVotesCapped = (structShort ? 1 : 0) + (rejShort ? 1 : 0) + (zoneShort ? 1 : 0) + (sessShort ? 1 : 0)
longVotesRaw  = (brkLong  ? 1 : 0) + (bosLong  ? 1 : 0) + (srLong  ? 1 : 0) + (sweepLong  ? 1 : 0) + (obLong  ? 1 : 0) + (fvLong  ? 1 : 0) + (orbLong  ? 1 : 0)
shortVotesRaw = (brkShort ? 1 : 0) + (bosShort ? 1 : 0) + (srShort ? 1 : 0) + (sweepShort ? 1 : 0) + (obShort ? 1 : 0) + (fvShort ? 1 : 0) + (orbShort ? 1 : 0)
longVotes  = capFamilies ? longVotesCapped  : longVotesRaw
shortVotes = capFamilies ? shortVotesCapped : shortVotesRaw

longOk  = inSession and volOk and volSurgeOk and deltaOkLong and longVotes  >= minConfirmations and (not blockOnOpposition or shortVotes == 0)
shortOk = inSession and volOk and volSurgeOk and deltaOkShort and shortVotes >= minConfirmations and (not blockOnOpposition or longVotes  == 0)

// The level the trade is measured from, most specific first. A zone edge is
// a price band someone actually defended; a range high is the loosest of
// them, so it is the fallback rather than the default.
float longLevel = na
if obLong
    longLevel := obLevelLong
else if fvLong
    longLevel := fvLevelLong
else if (sweepLong or srLong) and not na(lastPL)
    longLevel := lastPL
else if orbLong and not na(orbHigh)
    longLevel := orbHigh
else if structLong and not na(structLevelLong)
    longLevel := structLevelLong

float shortLevel = na
if obShort
    shortLevel := obLevelShort
else if fvShort
    shortLevel := fvLevelShort
else if (sweepShort or srShort) and not na(lastPH)
    shortLevel := lastPH
else if orbShort and not na(orbLow)
    shortLevel := orbLow
else if structShort and not na(structLevelShort)
    shortLevel := structLevelShort

// ------------------------------------------------------------ entries
flat = strategy.position_size == 0
var int pendingSince = na
var string pendingId = na

alertMsg(string action) =>
    '{"secret":"' + alertSecret + '","action":"' + action +
     '","symbol":"{{ticker}}","quantity":' + str.tostring(alertQty) +
     ',"price":"{{close}}","bar_time":"{{time}}","fired_at":"{{timenow}}"}'

var float plannedStop = na
canEnter = flat and na(pendingSince) and atrOk and barstate.isconfirmed

if canEnter and longOk and not na(longLevel)
    limitPrice = longLevel + entryAtrMult * atr
    // A buy limit at or above the market is a market order wearing a limit
    // order's name: it fills instantly at the worse price.
    if limitPrice < close
        plannedStop := longLevel - stopAtrMult * atr
        strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, limit=limitPrice, alert_message=alertMsg("buy"))
        pendingSince := bar_index
        pendingId := "L"

if canEnter and shortOk and not na(shortLevel)
    limitPrice = shortLevel - entryAtrMult * atr
    if limitPrice > close
        plannedStop := shortLevel + stopAtrMult * atr
        strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, limit=limitPrice, alert_message=alertMsg("sell"))
        pendingSince := bar_index
        pendingId := "S"

// An unfilled order left alive fills in some future bar whose setup has
// nothing to do with the signal it is attributed to.
if not na(pendingSince) and strategy.position_size == 0 and bar_index - pendingSince >= orderExpiryBars
    strategy.cancel(pendingId)
    pendingSince := na
    pendingId := na
    plannedStop := na

if strategy.position_size != 0
    pendingSince := na
    pendingId := na

// ----------------------------------------------------- stop management
var float stopLevel = na
var float entryR = na
var bool beLocked = false
var float runExtreme = na

justOpened = strategy.position_size != 0 and strategy.position_size[1] == 0
if justOpened
    entryPrice = strategy.position_avg_price
    isLong = strategy.position_size > 0
    rawStop = na(plannedStop) ? (isLong ? entryPrice - stopAtrMult * atr : entryPrice + stopAtrMult * atr) : plannedStop
    // A limit order fills at its price OR BETTER. Price gapping through a
    // buy limit can fill the long BELOW its own structural stop, leaving the
    // stop above the entry — an instant exit that books a loss looking like
    // the strategy failing when it is an unhandled fill.
    stopLevel := isLong ? math.min(rawStop, entryPrice - 0.25 * atr) : math.max(rawStop, entryPrice + 0.25 * atr)
    entryR := math.abs(entryPrice - stopLevel)
    beLocked := false
    runExtreme := isLong ? high : low

if strategy.position_size > 0
    runExtreme := na(runExtreme) ? high : math.max(runExtreme, high)
    entryPrice = strategy.position_avg_price
    if not beLocked and not na(entryR) and entryR > 0 and close >= entryPrice + breakevenR * entryR
        beLocked := true
        stopLevel := entryPrice
    if beLocked and atrOk and useTrailing
        // Trail only ratchets up. A stop that can loosen is not a stop.
        stopLevel := math.max(nz(stopLevel, entryPrice), runExtreme - trailAtrMult * atr)
    tpLong = takeProfitR > 0 and not na(entryR) ? entryPrice + takeProfitR * entryR : na
    if not na(stopLevel)
        strategy.exit("L-x", from_entry="L", stop=stopLevel, limit=tpLong, alert_message=alertMsg("exit"))

if strategy.position_size < 0
    runExtreme := na(runExtreme) ? low : math.min(runExtreme, low)
    entryPrice = strategy.position_avg_price
    if not beLocked and not na(entryR) and entryR > 0 and close <= entryPrice - breakevenR * entryR
        beLocked := true
        stopLevel := entryPrice
    if beLocked and atrOk and useTrailing
        stopLevel := math.min(nz(stopLevel, entryPrice), runExtreme + trailAtrMult * atr)
    tpShort = takeProfitR > 0 and not na(entryR) ? entryPrice - takeProfitR * entryR : na
    if not na(stopLevel)
        strategy.exit("S-x", from_entry="S", stop=stopLevel, limit=tpShort, alert_message=alertMsg("exit"))

if strategy.position_size == 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0
    stopLevel := na
    entryR := na
    beLocked := false
    runExtreme := na
    plannedStop := na

// -------------------------------------------------------------- plots
plot(useBreakout ? rangeHigh : na, "Range high", color=color.new(color.gray, 50), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(useBreakout ? rangeLow : na, "Range low", color=color.new(color.gray, 50), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(lastPH, "Swing high", color=color.new(color.orange, 30), style=plot.style_circles)
plot(lastPL, "Swing low", color=color.new(color.blue, 30), style=plot.style_circles)
plot(strategy.position_size != 0 ? stopLevel : na, "Stop", color=beLocked ? color.lime : color.red, style=plot.style_linebr)

plotshape(longOk  and flat, "Long signal",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.teal,   size=size.tiny)
plotshape(shortOk and flat, "Short signal", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.maroon, size=size.tiny)
plotchar(bosLong or bosShort,     "BOS",   "B", location.top, color.new(color.gray, 40), size=size.tiny)
plotchar(sweepLong or sweepShort, "Sweep", "S", location.bottom, color.new(color.yellow, 30), size=size.tiny)
plot(useOrb ? orbHigh : na, "ORB high", color=color.new(color.purple, 20), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
plot(useOrb ? orbLow : na, "ORB low", color=color.new(color.purple, 20), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
// A break waiting out its hold. Visible because "why is there no signal
// on that obvious break" should be answerable from the chart.
plotchar(not na(armBar), "Break on hold", "·", location.top, color.new(color.aqua, 30), size=size.tiny)

// A signal whose retest price was already through the market is skipped
// rather than filled at the market. Marked, because a triangle with no
// trade after it and nothing explaining why is how a script stops being
// trusted.
skippedLong  = canEnter and longOk  and not na(longLevel)  and longLevel  + entryAtrMult * atr >= close
skippedShort = canEnter and shortOk and not na(shortLevel) and shortLevel - entryAtrMult * atr <= close
plotshape(skippedLong or skippedShort, "Signal skipped (no retest room)", shape.xcross,
     location.top, color.new(color.gray, 40), size=size.tiny)

// --------------------------------------------------------- vote table
// Declared at global scope: Pine does not allow a function declaration
// inside a conditional block, and putting this one inside `if
// barstate.islast` is a compile error rather than a subtle bug.
voteCell(table t, int r, string name, bool l, bool s, bool on) =>
    table.cell(t, 0, r, name, text_size=size.tiny,
         text_color=on ? color.gray : color.new(color.gray, 65))
    table.cell(t, 1, r, not on ? "off" : l ? "LONG" : s ? "SHORT" : "-", text_size=size.tiny,
         text_color=not on ? color.new(color.gray, 65) : l ? color.teal : s ? color.maroon : color.gray)

// A solo count of zero is the interesting case: the strategy fired but
// never alone in its family, so it never changed a vote. Coloured rather
// than left to be spotted.
statCell(table t, int r, int fired, int solo, bool on) =>
    txt = not on ? "" : str.tostring(fired) + " / " + str.tostring(solo)
    col = not on ? color.new(color.gray, 65) : solo == 0 and fired > 0 ? color.orange : color.gray
    table.cell(t, 2, r, txt, text_size=size.tiny, text_color=col)

var table votes = table.new(position.top_right, 3, 13, border_width=1)
if barstate.islast
    table.cell(votes, 0, 0, "Family / strategy", text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(votes, 1, 0, str.tostring(longVotes) + "L / " + str.tostring(shortVotes) + "S",
         text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(votes, 2, 0, "fired/solo", text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.white)
    voteCell(votes, 1, "STRUCTURE", structLong, structShort, useBreakout or useBos)
    voteCell(votes, 2, "  range breakout", brkLong, brkShort, useBreakout)
    statCell(votes, 2, nBrk, sBrk, useBreakout)
    voteCell(votes, 3, "  BOS", bosLong, bosShort, useBos)
    statCell(votes, 3, nBos, sBos, useBos)
    voteCell(votes, 4, "REJECTION", rejLong, rejShort, useSR or useSweep)
    voteCell(votes, 5, "  S/R pushback", srLong, srShort, useSR)
    statCell(votes, 5, nSr, sSr, useSR)
    voteCell(votes, 6, "  liquidity sweep", sweepLong, sweepShort, useSweep)
    statCell(votes, 6, nSweep, sSweep, useSweep)
    voteCell(votes, 7, "ZONE", zoneLong, zoneShort, useZones or useFvg)
    voteCell(votes, 8, "  order block", obLong, obShort, useZones)
    statCell(votes, 8, nOb, sOb, useZones)
    voteCell(votes, 9, "  fair value gap", fvLong, fvShort, useFvg)
    statCell(votes, 9, nFv, sFv, useFvg)
    voteCell(votes, 10, "SESSION", sessLong, sessShort, useOrb)
    voteCell(votes, 11, "  opening range", orbLong, orbShort, useOrb)
    statCell(votes, 11, nOrb, sOrb, useOrb)
    table.cell(votes, 0, 12, "Need", text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.gray)
    table.cell(votes, 1, 12, str.tostring(minConfirmations) + (capFamilies ? " of 4 families" : " uncapped") +
         (useTrailing or takeProfitR > 0 ? "" : "  NO EXIT") +
         (holdBars > 0 ? "  hold " + str.tostring(holdBars) : ""),
         text_size=size.tiny, text_color=useTrailing or takeProfitR > 0 ? color.gray : color.red)
